{"id":"chapter-001","n":1,"title":{"en":[["Preface","","t"]],"zh":[["序","xù","t"],["言","yán","t"]],"ja":[["序","じょ","t"]]},"p":[{"id":"kappa-akutagawa-s001-p00001","src":"This is the story that a patient in a certain mental hospital—Patient No. 23—tells to anyone who will listen. He must be over thirty by now. Yet at first glance, he looks every inch a youthful madman. The experiences of the first half of his life—but no, none of that matters. He merely sat there, clasping both knees and occasionally glancing out of the window. (Beyond its iron bars stood a single oak, not even a dead leaf remaining on it, its branches spread against a snow-laden sky.) With Dr. S, the hospital director, and me as his audience, he went on telling this story at great length. Not that he spoke without gestures. Whenever he said, for example, that he was “astonished,” he would suddenly fling his head back. …I believe I have transcribed his story with considerable accuracy. Should anyone remain dissatisfied with my account, they may visit the S Mental Hospital in the village of ××, outside Tokyo. Patient No. 23, younger in appearance than his years, will first bow politely and point to an unpadded chair. Then, with a melancholy smile, he will quietly repeat this story. And at the end—I remember the look on his face when he finished telling me this story. The moment he sits up at the end, he will begin brandishing his fists and roar at anyone before him: —“Get out! You scoundrel! You too must be a stupid, jealous, obscene, brazen, conceited, cruel, self-serving animal. Get out! You scoundrel!”","u":[{"en":[["This","","a"]," ",["is","","p"]," ",["the","","a"]," ",["story","","o"]," ",["that","","f"]," ",["a","","a"]," ",["patient","","t"]," ",["in","","f"]," ",["a","","a"]," ",["certain","","a"]," ",["mental","","a"]," ",["hospital","","t"],"—",["Patient","","t"]," ",["No","","t"],"."," ",["23","","a"],"—",["tells","","t"]," ",["to","","f"]," ",["anyone","","d"]," ",["who","","f"]," ",["wil